{title: Paper Lanterns}
{artist: The Hollow Pines}

{start_of_intro: Intro}
[G]  [D/F#]  [Em]  [C]
{end_of_intro}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[G]Paper lanterns on [D/F#]the water
[Em]Floating where the ri[C]ver bends
[G]You were laughing a[D/F#]t the thunder
[Em]Like the storm wa[C]s just a friend
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[C]Let them drif[G]t, let them go
[D]Every light we did[Em]n't hold
[C]Burning low, [G]burning slow
[D]Somewhere down the [G]road
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[G]Now the jetty's f[D/F#]ull of strangers
[Em]And the summer's [C]packed away
[G]I still find you in [D/F#]the embers
[Em]Of a match I str[C]uck today
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[C]Let them drif[G]t, let them go
[D]Every light we did[Em]n't hold
[C]Burning low, [G]burning slow
[D]Somewhere down the [G]road
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
[Am]Maybe light wa[Em]s never meant to stay
[Am]Maybe that's the w[D]hole of it
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_outro: Outro}
[G]  [D/F#]  [Em]  [C]  [G]
{end_of_outro}
